Spec: Day dialog
Purpose:
  Admin-only editing of a single day. A `<dialog>` modal lets the admin add a Holiday, a NoTeachWeek, a Conference or
  a Lesson, and HTMX swaps the updated wall planner, or the realization weekly table when the dialog is opened from
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd, into the page without a reload. Orchestrates ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd, ../holidays/holidays.sdd, ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd and
  ../conferences/conferences.sdd services and renders through ../semester/semester.sdd's and
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd's views, so it owns a view.py and routes.py only.

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../auth/auth.sdd
  ../semester/semester.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd
  ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd
  ../conferences/conferences.sdd

Exposes:
  ./view.py's @dialog_container, @GRID_ID, @WEEK_TABLE_ID, @CONTAINER_ID and @DIALOG_PATH: the container, the wall
    planner grid id, the weekly table id, the swap targets and the dialog path that ../semester/semester.sdd's and
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's view.py need to render their admin affordances.
  ./view.py's @time_select with @START_TIME_LATEST and @END_TIME_LATEST: the `HH:MM` dropdown builder and its
    start-time and end-time bounds, which ../realizations/realizations.sdd's Lesson edit dialog uses too.
  ./view.py's @HOLIDAY_PATH and @NO_TEACH_WEEK_PATH with @holiday_path, @holiday_delete_path, @no_teach_week_path
    and @no_teach_week_delete_path: the edit and delete routes ./routes.py registers and ./view.py's forms post to.
  ./view.py's @CONFERENCE_PATH with @conference_path and @conference_delete_path: the edit and delete routes
    ./routes.py registers for a ../conferences/conferences.sdd Conference and ./view.py's forms post to.

Must:
  Clicking a day row in ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner opens a `<dialog>` for the admin and does nothing for
  unauthenticated visitors, who are shown no day-row trigger at all.
  ./view.py exposes @dialog_container, the empty element the containing view renders once; every dialog response is
  the bare `<dialog>` that is swapped into it, never the container itself, so a swap cannot nest a duplicate id.
  The dialog offers one tab per kind of entry the admin can add on the clicked date, in the order Lesson, Holiday,
    NoTeachWeek, Conference, and opens on the Lesson tab because a Lesson is the most commonly added entry. Switching
    tabs re-renders the dialog in place through HTMX.
  The dialog can also be opened from ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly table through a `realization_id`
    query parameter; then the Holiday and Lesson forms replace the date field with ../shared/shared.sdd's
    @day_calendar, a Monday-first month grid of the clicked day's month with that day's week Monday checked, so the
    admin picks the date on a Finnish week instead of a browser date picker that may start its week on Sunday, and the
    Lesson form defaults to that realization.
  The Holiday form takes a title. The Conference form takes a title and says that a conference spanning several days
    is stored as one entry per day, per ../conferences/conferences.sdd. The NoTeachWeek form takes a week number,
    prefilled with the clicked date's ISO week and editable, and a title, prefilled with
    ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd's shared default title and editable.
  The Lesson form takes a CourseRealization from a dropdown listing only that Semester's realizations, a topic and
  notes, and, side by side on one row, a start time and an end time, each chosen from a dropdown of 24-hour `HH:MM`
  values on a 15-minute grid: the start time runs from `08:00` to `20:45` and the end time from `08:00` to `21:00`.
  It reports that the Semester has no realization instead of offering an unusable form.
  Each form is an HTMX request whose response is the whole re-rendered wall planner, or the whole re-rendered
  weekly table when a `realization_id` was given, since one entry can change more than the clicked row: a
  NoTeachWeek tints all five of its Monday-to-Friday rows.
  That response is the bare `semester-grid` element rendered through ../semester/semester.sdd's @semester_grid or
  the bare @WEEK_TABLE_ID element rendered through ../realizations/realizations.sdd's view, never the dialog
  container, so the containing page keeps its appearance and renders the container exactly once.
  A submission that the underlying service rejects, or whose form field cannot be parsed, leaves the entry unstored
  and re-renders the dialog with a validation message and the values the admin submitted.
  Opening the dialog and every submission are rejected by the ../auth/auth.sdd guard for non-admin sessions.
  When the clicked date already holds a Holiday, the Holiday tab offers that Holiday's edit form instead of the add
    form: its title and its date through ../shared/shared.sdd's @day_calendar are prefilled, and it posts to
    `/day/dialog/holidays/{holiday_id}`. When the clicked date already holds a
    ../conferences/conferences.sdd Conference, its tab offers that Conference's edit form exactly as the Holiday tab
    does, posting to `/day/dialog/conferences/{conference_id}`. When the clicked date falls inside a NoTeachWeek, the
    NoTeachWeek tab offers that week's edit form instead, prefilled with its stored week number rather than the
    clicked date's ISO week and with its title, posting to `/day/dialog/no-teach-week/{no_teach_week_id}`. A date no
    NoTeachWeek blocks still offers the add form.
  The blocked week is found through the clicked date's own Monday, so a Saturday or Sunday of a blocked week edits
    that same week instead of offering the add form, which that Semester would reject as a duplicate.
  Each edit form carries a `Delete` control that confirms, naming the entry and its date, before removing it
    through `/day/dialog/holidays/{holiday_id}/delete`, `/day/dialog/conferences/{conference_id}/delete` or
    `/day/dialog/no-teach-week/{no_teach_week_id}/delete`, which write through ../holidays/holidays.sdd's
    @HolidayService.delete_holiday, ../conferences/conferences.sdd's @ConferenceService.delete_conference and
    ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd's @NoTeachWeekService.delete_no_teach_week.
  An edit writes through @HolidayService.update_holiday, @ConferenceService.update_conference and
    @NoTeachWeekService.update_no_teach_week and re-renders the same containing view an added entry does; a rejected
    edit or delete leaves the stored entry as it was and re-renders the dialog with the validation message and the
    values the admin submitted.
  The dialog edits only the Holiday, the Conference and the NoTeachWeek; a Lesson is edited from
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly table, so no Lesson appears here for editing.
  This package crosses into ../semester/semester.sdd only through its view.py and services.py, never through its
    domain.py or ports.py, so the pair is the mutual dependency ../architecture.sdd permits.

Scenario: Admin adds a conference
  Given the admin is logged in and views the semester view
  When the admin clicks a day row, chooses the Conference tab, enters a title and submits
  Then the dialog closes and the day row shows that title in purple without a page reload

Scenario: Admin edits an existing conference
  Given a Conference is stored on a date the admin clicks in ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner
  When the admin changes its title or date in the dialog's Conference tab and saves
  Then the new date shows the new title in purple and the previous one no longer shows it

Scenario: Admin adds a lesson
  Given the admin is logged in and views the semester view
  When the admin clicks a day row, chooses a course realization, enters a start time, an end time, a topic and notes
  and submits
  Then the dialog closes and the day row shows a new colored square without a page reload

Scenario: Visitor clicks a day
  Given the visitor is not logged in
  When the visitor clicks a day row
  Then no dialog opens

Scenario: Admin adds a holiday
  Given the admin is logged in and views the semester view
  When the admin clicks a day row, types a title and submits
  Then the dialog closes and the day row shows the title tinted as a Holiday

Scenario: Admin blocks a week
  Given the admin is logged in and views the semester view
  When the admin clicks a day row, chooses the NoTeachWeek tab and submits the prefilled week
  Then all five of that week's weekdays are tinted and titled without a page reload

Scenario: Rejected entry is not stored
  Given the admin submits an entry the underlying service rejects
  When the response arrives
  Then the dialog stays open with a validation message and the entry is not stored

Scenario: Admin edits an existing holiday
  Given a Holiday is stored on a date the admin clicks in ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner
  When the admin changes its title or date in the dialog's Holiday tab and saves
  Then that day row shows the new title without a page reload

Scenario: Admin removes a no-teach week
  Given a NoTeachWeek blocks a week of the shown Semester
  When the admin confirms the delete control on a day inside that week
  Then the week's Monday-to-Friday rows are no longer tinted, with the other NoTeachWeeks left in place

Scenario: Admin adds a lesson from the weekly view
  Given the admin is logged in and views a realization's weekly table
  When the admin clicks a week row, chooses a course realization, picks the date on the Monday-first calendar, enters
    a start time, an end time and a topic and submits
  Then the weekly table re-renders in place with the new lesson

Tasks:
  [x] Implement the dialog, its tab per kind and the holiday form with the HTMX grid swap
  [x] Implement the lesson form
  [x] Implement the NoTeachWeek form, prefilled with the clicked day's ISO week
  [x] Implement editing of existing entries for the Holiday and the NoTeachWeek, prefilled with their stored values
    and deletable through a confirming control, leaving the Lesson to ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly table
  [x] Let the admin edit and remove a Semester's NoTeachWeeks through ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd
  [x] Open the dialog from ../realizations/realizations.sdd's week rows, with the Monday-first month calendar for the
    Holiday and Lesson forms and the weekly-table swap
  [x] Render the date through ../shared/shared.sdd's @day_calendar instead of a browser date picker, so the dialog's
    week starts on Monday in every locale
  [x] Offer the Lesson form's start and end times side by side as @time_select dropdowns of 15-minute values from
    `08:00` to `20:45` and `21:00` instead of free-text inputs
  [x] Add the Conference tab with its add form and with the prefilled edit and delete controls for the Conference
    already on the clicked date, per ../conferences/conferences.sdd, and route its three guarded writes
